{"title":"Tribonacci sequence","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Tribonacci sequence</b> is a varation of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fibonacci_sequence\" title=\"Fibonacci sequence\">fibonacci sequence</a>, where each term after the third is equal to the sum of the three previous terms. Starting with the initial values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12cf6f6ac7aa6fd3495881bbe59b90472778fd43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 0, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, the first 18 values of the sequence are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c2e8944c32d4f780c47d86859aa2b933dfc169f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 4, 7, 13, 24, 44, 81, 149, 274, 504, 927, 1705, 3136, 5768$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"494\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>The numbers in the tribonacci sequence are known as tribonacci numbers. Thus, using the definition, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924308a4de890f9849585b4bc8e86570917789d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> represents the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> tribonacci number, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/537daa1856a48ab6bff37c475d172b00b6a8eaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n} + T_{n + 1} + T_{n + 2} = T_{n + 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tribonacci_constant\">Tribonacci constant</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tribonacci_sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Tribonacci constant\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <b>tribonacci constant</b>, like how the fibonacci sequence has the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Golden_ratio\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Golden ratio\">golden ratio</a>, is equal to the ratio in which adjacent tribonacci numbers tend. For instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0eabf0ff40d7c37208e01e01632e2a3b0a939dfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81}{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e692ebb526aab500d2437514984de399672761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>It is equal to the real root of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d29060eacbf01853c973699451b00f7c589532a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{3} - x^{2} - x - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_Tribonacci_Constant\">Proof of Tribonacci Constant</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tribonacci_sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of Tribonacci Constant\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Uses_of_the_Tribonacci_Sequence\">Uses of the Tribonacci Sequence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tribonacci_sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Uses of the Tribonacci Sequence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Tribonacci_sequence&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNe